g.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:fb730d179cda15553673d1ed775dfc6cd1f096cb8cdfb103615509462ce10794\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"for f in host/*.sh scripts/run-tp2.sh; do bash -n \\\"$f\\\"; done && grep -q 'PYTHONHASHSEED=0' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'thunderbolt0' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'ExecStopPost' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && ! grep -q 'WantedBy' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v\"],\"description\":\"Env doctrine present, units teardown-safe, all scripts syntax-clean, host tests pass.\",\"id\":\"host-doctrine\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"host\",\"scripts/run-tp2.sh\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"One command stands the pair service; one command tears it down; failure cannot strand ranks\",\"First light produces the four receipts the ladder grades\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Write the host/ tooling and scripts/run-tp2.sh per spec claims 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5 and 6.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4, #r6), composing the disciplines in specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 5 and specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md section 5. host/fn-env.sh: PYTHONHASHSEED=0; PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85; HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT=1; inductor and triton cache dirs under the state directory, never tmpfs; NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME set ONLY to the Thunderbolt rails that carry a routable /30 IP (rail 0 thunderbolt0/10.99.0.x is guaranteed; rail 1 thunderbolt1 is trained-but-IP-unconfigured today per dotfiles modules/lowlat-cluster.nix and MUST NOT be listed until it has a peer IP — a peerless link-local rail in the list hangs RCCL bootstrap; the env file computes this from `ip -br addr` at write time and logs which rails it chose, rather than hardcoding both); NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 UNCONDITIONALLY (an ibverbs device now exists on the rails from the pre-arm bake; without this pin RCCL autodetects verbs and silently rides unproven RDMA — sockets are the transport of record until the attended morning A/B, evidence host/rdma/ab-protocol.md); VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_; VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1; a loud comment forbidding exports of engine defaults read through is-set probes. host/fn-cluster-up.sh: podman on both nodes (worker over ssh on the wire), distributed head on the coordinator and worker join, worker python pool capped small, a hard two-GPU gate before serve, then the serve process at tensor-parallel size 2 with eager execution, model directory /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8, served name flashnext; reap stranded serve processes before start and gate on zero residue. host/fn-cluster-down.sh: idempotent teardown both nodes. host/fn-preflight.sh: byte-diff of both ranks' FN_ env, latency-hold device read on both ends, per-rail link-speed record, round-trip probe on both rails. host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service: oneshot, RemainAfterExit, ExecStopPost teardown, no install section. scripts/run-tp2.sh: preflight, up, two greedy 300-token completions byte-compared, residency read after 50 warmed decode tokens (GTT per rank from sysfs plus process RSS plus table page-cache residency), fidelity capture (fixed-prompt losses and frontier logits under results/), then a 262144-context probe, writing receipts tp2.json, residency.json, fidelity.json, context.json per the receipts-verify.py schema. Extend tests/test_repo_invariants.py-adjacent coverage with tests/test_host_tooling.py asserting the env file carries the doctrine lines and unit files carry ExecStopPost and no WantedBy install. Boundaries: touch only host/, scripts/run-tp2.sh, and tests/.\",\"id\":\"host-tooling\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4\",\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/stage-weights.sh\",\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d\",\"title\":\"Pair-service orchestration: env doctrine, cluster up/down, first-light runner\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"e4ac78a9ba2a84aca3baec47a4698602a2f3b850\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-57f87640bc5b/host-tooling\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"host\",\"scripts/run-tp2.sh\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/host-tooling-ab66c582012f053f\",\"taskId\":\"host-tooling\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"PRE-DISPATCH STEER (overseer, arm-time — fold into your first brief). Semantic traps your grep gate cannot catch; all are hard requirements: (1) NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME must be COMPUTED from `ip -br addr` — only rails that actually carry a routable IP. Rail 1 (thunderbolt1) is trained but IP-UNCONFIGURED (169.254.x link-local, no peer): hardcoding both rails passes the grep and hangs RCCL bootstrap. In practice only thunderbolt0 (10.99.0.x /30) qualifies. (2) NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 UNCONDITIONALLY in host/fn-env.sh — not conditional on device detection. ibverbs devices exist on BOTH nodes by design (usb4_rdma0 + usb4_rdma5); without the pin RCCL autodetects verbs and silently rides the unproven RDMA path. Sockets are the transport of record this run. (3) NEVER export a probe-read engine default: VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM, VLLM_MOE_USE_DEEP_GEMM, VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER* are read via is_set() probes — exporting the default diverts the oracle into a hard raise (spec F.9). (4) Receipts must match scripts/receipts-verify.py EXACTLY — run it against your own output before declaring done. (5) Worker-side actions ride the ethernet wire (10.99.9.2), never a 10.99.0.x Thunderbolt rail — rails carry tensors only. (6) cluster-up is reap-then-gate: reap stale processes first, then gate on health, in that order.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:05:30.106Z\",\"id\":1,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-29T06:05:30.106Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/1\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[1],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":4,\"recheckedCursor\":4,\"registrationId\":\"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988646298}]}
