{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_17269b6595974ae4a3f15023","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service — the flashnext pair service.\n#\n# One command stands the pair (fn-cluster-up.sh), one command tears it down\n# (fn-cluster-down.sh). Oneshot with RemainAfterExit so the unit reflects\n# \"the pair is up\" while the serve process runs detached inside its\n# container; failure cannot strand ranks because StopPost tears down even\n# when ExecStart itself failed.\n#\n# Install with `systemctl --user link host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service`\n# from the repository root, then drive explicitly:\n#   systemctl --user start flashnext-pair    # stand the pair\n#   systemctl --user stop  flashnext-pair    # tear the pair down\n#\n# Type=oneshot + RemainAfterExit: ExecStart completes once the served name\n# answers on the API port; the unit stays active while the pair serves.\n# TimeoutStartSec covers a cold-kernel-cache bring-up (~25 min of LLVM plus\n# the weight load).\n[Unit]\nDescription=flashnext pair service — TP=2 vendor FP8 release on coordinator+worker\nAfter=network-online.target\nWants=network-online.target\n\n[Service]\nType=oneshot\nRemainAfterExit=yes\nTimeoutStartSec=45min\nTimeoutStopSec=5min\nExecStart=%h/mecattaf/flashnext/host/fn-cluster-up.sh\nExecStop=%h/mecattaf/flashnext/host/fn-cluster-down.sh\n# ExecStop does not run when ExecStart itself fails; StopPost does, so a\n# failed bring-up still tears the pair down instead of leaving ray daemons\n# and half-up containers behind a 'failed' wrapper. fn-cluster-down.sh is\n# idempotent, so the Stop+StopPost double call is deliberate and safe.\nExecStopPost=%h/mecattaf/flashnext/host/fn-cluster-down.sh\n\n# Deliberately NO [Install] section: the model takes tens of minutes to load\n# and claims both GPUs, so the stack comes up only on an explicit start by\n# the operator or the overnight overseer — never at boot, never via WantedBy.\n","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling/host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service"}}}}
