{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Make the script executable and run the acceptance criteria:\n\n1. chmod +x host/*.sh scripts/run-tp2.sh\n2. bash -n on everything\n3. The entire acceptance argv\n4. python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v\n5. The full unittest discover (repo-tests gate) to confirm nothing regressed\n6. receipts-verify is still clean\n\nOne concern regarding test_fn_env_rails_are_computed_not_hardcoded: `assertNotRegex(self.env, r\"^\\s*export NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=thunderbolt\")` — my line is `export NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=\"${NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME:-$(fn_choose_rails)}\"` — starts with `export NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=\"${...` — does not match the `=thunderbolt` pattern. Good.\n\nAlso `assertIn(\"169.254\", self.env)` — it's present. Good.\n\ntest_cluster_up_reaps_before_it_gates: \"reap_serve_node\" appears at definition time — before \"ray start\". Wait, does \"ray start\" appear inside a comment before the reap definition? Header comment: \"3. Ray head on the coordinator, worker join\" — no \"ray start\" literal in the header. First occurrence of \"ray start\" literal: the actual command `podman exec \"$FN_CONTAINER\" ray start --head`. Occurrences of \"reap_serve_node\": function definition (after the header). Header has \"REAP stranded serve processes\" but no literal \"reap_serve_node\". Order OK: function definition is around line 30, before the ray start line.\n\n\"zero residue\" — appears in `log \"reap gate passed: zero residue on both nodes\"`. Good.\n\"two-GPU gate\" — appears in log + comments. Good.\n\nrunner.replace(\"'\", '\"') — my heredoc uses double quotes `\"step\": \"tp2\"` in python, so the literal `\"step\": \"tp2\"` exists directly in the file. Good.\n\nNow I'll run the checks."}}
