{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The receipt schema has been verified bidirectionally: valid receipts pass, and non-engaged mmap probes fail with an error.\n\nA few more review passes on the script:\n\n1. fn-cluster-up.sh — the worker container startup: I used `worker \"podman rm -f ... && podman run -d ...\"` — a single ssh argument string, no problem.\n\n2. fn-cluster-up.sh: `log \"reap: coordinator\"` comes before the `residue=\"$(reap_serve_node)\"` call — reap_serve_node is already defined at that point (function definitions appear at the top of the file). Verify the order within the file: section-1 comment, reap_serve_node definition, then log + call. Yes.\n\n3. fn-preflight.sh — `worker \"cat > '$REMOTE_TMP/fn-env.sh'\" < \"$SCRIPT_DIR/fn-env.sh\"` — REMOTE_TMP is obtained from `worker 'mktemp -d'`. No problem.\n\n4. fn-preflight.sh check_hold: `record \"hold_$node\" \"$probe\"` — probe format is \"active|0\". The receipt python splits it. Good.\n\n5. Potential set -e pitfall in fn-preflight.sh: `ping -q ... | tail -n1 | awk ...` inside $( ) — if ping fails (no route), the pipeline returns the awk exit code — the awk on empty input prints nothing, exit code 0? awk with no input exits with 0. printf '%s %s' gets rtt=\"\" → \"${rtt:-probe-failed}\" → \"probe-failed\" → fail branch. Good.\n\nHmm wait, in rtt_probe_node: `rtt=\"$(ping ... 2>/dev/null | tail -n1 | awk -F'[/ ]' '{ printf \"%d\", $8 * 1000 }')\"` — under `set -euo pipefail`... this is inside a command substitution assigned to a local variable? This is inside a function called via $( ) from the driver; pipefail: ping's exit code is non-zero → pipeline fails → but this is part of `rtt=\"$(...)\"` inside the function; under set -e, a failed command substitution in an assignment = the function exits. The rtt_probe_node function itself runs on the remote side via ssh `bash -c \"$(declare -f); rtt_probe_node\"` — remote bash does NOT have set -e (ssh runs the default shell without -e). Locally (coordinator), fn-preflight.sh has set -euo pipefail; `rtts=\"$(rtt_probe_node)\"` — inside rtt_probe_node, does the failing pipeline assignment cause an abort under set -e? A failing command substitution inside an assignment: `rtt=\"$(pipeline)\"` — assignment exit status = command substitution status → non-zero → set -e fires → fn-preflight aborts without a receipt. Bad for rails that are down... but the rails have routable IPs (rail0) and rail1 is skipped early. ping to a live rail succeeds. Edge case: if rail0 exists but peer is unreachable → abort instead of a fail receipt. Mitigation: append `|| true` to the pipeline inside the substitution. Let me patch it:\n\nrtt=\"$(ping ... | tail -n1 | awk ... || true)\" — pipefail and || true → overall no problem.\n\nSimilarly in fn_choose_rails (fn-env.sh): `addr=\"$(ip ... | grep -oE ... | grep -Ev ... | head -n1 || true)\"` — there's already `|| true`. Good. Though when sourcing fn-env.sh in a set -e context: guarded by || true ✓.\n\nfn-cluster-up.sh: `gpus_total=\"$(podman exec ... | awk ... )\" || true` ✓ guarded.\n\nfn-preflight.sh: the latency_hold_probe `val=\"$(od ... || true)\"` guarded ✓; `unit=\"$(systemctl is-active ... || true)\"` ✓.\n\nenv dump: `( set -a; source ... >/dev/null; env ) | grep -E ... | LC_ALL=C sort > file` — under pipefail, if grep finds nothing → exit code 1 → abort. grep will always find something (PYTHONHASHSEED etc.) ✓. Remote version runs over ssh without -e ✓.\n\nIn fn-cluster-up.sh, the worker env dump is a remote ssh string — no problem.\n\nAnother potential set -e problem in fn-preflight.sh: `speeds=\"$(rail_speeds)\"` — cat /sys speed file: `$(cat ... || echo down)` guarded ✓.\n\n`while read -r rail speed; do ... done <<< \"$speeds\"` — no problem.\n\nIn check_hold: early `return` inside a case under set -e — check_hold is called as a top-level command; returns only after record/fail; return status of the last command in fail() is... fail() ends with `status=fail` (assignment, exit code 0) ✓. Then `return` → check_hold returns 0 ✓.\n\n6. run-tp2.sh: `python3 - <<'PY' ... PY` with sys.exit(1) on step failure → set -e aborts the runner. The receipt has already been written before exit. Good.\n\n7. `export FN_METRICS=\"$TMP/rank_metrics.py\"` — used in the heredoc ✓.\n\n8. run-tp2.sh: bash variables RECEIPTS/FIDELITY_DIR are exported ✓ (RECEIPTS is now already exported; FIDELITY_DIR is exported before the fidelity step). FN_API is also exported ✓. Note though: the tp2 and residency heredocs use os.environ[\"RECEIPTS\"] — exported ✓.\n\n9. fn-cluster-up.sh `run_container` — `podman run -d ... >/dev/null` — podman prints the container ID; suppressed ✓. But note: `podman run` under set -e, if the image doesn't exist → aborts loudly ✓ (desired).\n\n10. Unit file: `Wants=network-online.target` and After — no problem for user units? network-online.target may not exist in the user manager; harmless (Wants doesn't fail). Keep it.\n\nApply the ping || true patch. Reconsidering: `ping -c 20 -i 0.05` — 20 pings at 50ms intervals ≈ 1 second. OK.\n\nAnother trap check: the env byte-diff compares the full doctrine env including NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME — both nodes compute thunderbolt0 → identical ✓. Note however that the env dump includes FN_STATE_DIR which contains $HOME — on both nodes $HOME=/home/tom ✓ identical.\n\nfn-env.sh does mkdir -p when sourced → creates directories on both nodes ✓ harmless.\n\nPotential issue: fn-env.sh's `return 1 2>/dev/null || exit 1` — if sourced without set -e from a script that has set -e (fn-cluster-up.sh sources with set -euo pipefail active): if rails are empty, `return 1` inside a sourced file returns from the sourced script — return exits the sourced file with status 1 → sourcing fails → cluster-up's set -e aborts. Good (loud). If EXECUTED directly (bash fn-env.sh), return outside a function errors → exit 1. ✓.\n\nNow apply the ping patch, then rerun the whole gate."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"One robustness fix: under `set -euo pipefail` in fn-preflight.sh, a failed ping pipeline would abort before the receipt is written. Guarding it:\n\n"}}
