{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now, to verify that the receipt-writing part works, let's do an end-to-end dry run of the report → receipt Python part of fn-preflight.sh. Either extract and run just the Python part with a synthetic report, or better yet, simulate the whole preflight on this machine using shims (ssh shim, fake sysfs, fake systemctl). This is heavier, but worthwhile since it lets us verify the script's plumbing (declare -f over ssh, record file, receipt JSON).\n\nPlan: create a sandbox PATH bin with the following:\n- ssh: runs the rest locally (exec bash -c \"$@\") — simulates a worker = same machine.\n- systemctl: prints \"active\" for is-active.\n- ping: prints canned stats.\n- ip: same shim as before.\n- od: prints 0.\n- sudo: exec \"$@\".\nFake /sys/class/net/thunderbolt0/speed — the check `[ -r /sys/class/net/$rail/speed ]` is a literal path again — can't be faked without sed. The rail_speeds function reads literal /sys/class/net — on this machine that results in \"absent\" — no problem, it gets recorded as absent. The RTT probe also uses a literal `ip -br -4 addr show dev thunderboltN` — but ip is shimmed, and the probe doesn't check for sysfs presence! rtt_probe_node runs `ip -br -4 addr show dev thunderbolt0` → shim returns an addr → pings the peer via the shimmed ping → records the rtt. The thunderbolt1 shim returns link-local → skipped as no-peer-ip.\n\n/dev/cpu_dma_latency: not readable by tom → falls back to `sudo -n od` → shim sudo → shim od prints 0. Actually, the [ -r /dev/cpu_dma_latency ] check is false → else branch with sudo -n od. Shim: `sudo` is exec \"${@#-n }\"... simplest is: cat > bin/sudo 'exec \"${@/-n/}\"' hmm. Let's just make sudo drop args: printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nshift\\nexec \"$@\"\\n' — sudo -n od ... → shift removes -n → exec od. Good.\n- od shim: regardless of args, prints \" 0\".\n\nThen run fn-preflight.sh with PATH override, RECEIPT → to a temp copy of the repo root? The script computes REPO_ROOT from SCRIPT_DIR/.. and writes to results/receipts/preflight.json — writing to results/ in the working tree is out of the write boundary for commits, but uncommitted scratch artifacts in the working tree pollute git status. Workaround: copy host/ into a sandbox directory structure $S/host + $S/results and run the copied script. The script is self-contained (sources fn-env.sh via SCRIPT_DIR).\n\nLet's run it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now an end-to-end dry run of `fn-preflight.sh` in a sandbox with shims for `ssh`, `ip`, `ping`, `systemctl`, `sudo`, `od`:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d37557d75ed0460aa1f8e5b5","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"set -e; S=$(mktemp -d); R=/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling\nmkdir -p \"$S/host\" \"$S/bin\"\ncp \"$R/host/fn-env.sh\" \"$R/host/fn-preflight.sh\" \"$S/host/\"\nsed -i 's|/sys/class/net/|'\"$S\"'/sysnet/|g' \"$S/host/fn-env.sh\"\nmkdir -p \"$S/sysnet/thunderbolt0\" \"$S/sysnet/thunderbolt1\"\ncat > \"$S/bin/ip\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *thunderbolt0*) echo \"thunderbolt0  UP  10.99.0.1/30\" ;;\n  *thunderbolt1*) echo \"thunderbolt1  UP  169.254.5.6/16\" ;;\nesac\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/ssh\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nshift; exec bash -c \"$*\"\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/systemctl\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n[ \"$1\" = is-active ] && echo active\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/ping\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\necho \"PING ignored\"; echo \"rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 58.0/77.2/112.0/9.1 ms\"\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/sudo\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nshift; exec \"$@\"\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/od\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\necho \"           0\"\nEOF\nchmod +x \"$S/bin/\"*\nPATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$S/home\" bash \"$S/host/fn-preflight.sh\" 2>&1 | tail -12\necho \"=== receipt ===\"; cat \"$S/results/receipts/preflight.json\"\nrm -rf \"$S\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","p