{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"All 5 Python blocks (tp2 client, rank_metrics, residency driver, fidelity, context) can be compiled.\n\nWait — blk2 is the rank_metrics.py written by `cat > \"$TMP/rank_metrics.py\" <<'PY'` — that's also quoted PY. Good, all 5 compile.\n\nNow, one more full review of run-tp2.sh for correctness:\n\n1. In the context heredoc, `PARAGRAPH * int(...)` — repetition of a large string is fine.\n2. `est_chars_per_token = 4.2` — the PARAGRAPH text is English, but it might actually be closer to 3.8–4.5 characters/token for this tokenizer family. Undershoot and re-pad once — reasonable.\n3. In decode_tps, `(tokens - 1) / (t_last - t_first)` — first-token latency is partially excluded; consistent across both arms.\n\nOne more check: the tp2 heredoc of run-tp2.sh — RECEIPTS env var: exported ✓ (after my fix). Let me grep to confirm the export line ordering: `export RECEIPTS` is before the first python. ✓.\n\nAlso FN_API is exported after cluster-up — the tp2/residency/fidelity/context heredocs all use it ✓.\n\nfn-cluster-up.sh concerns: `podman exec \"$FN_CONTAINER\" ray status 2>/dev/null | awk ...` — under pipefail, if ray status fails → the pipeline fails → `|| true` is attached to the assignment ✓ (`gpus_total=\"$(...)\" || true`).\n\nfn-cluster-up.sh: the ssh string for the worker container has `\\` line continuation inside the double-quoted ssh command — valid shell text that runs remotely ✓. Note: `--env-file '$REMOTE_TMP/env.list'` — $REMOTE_TMP is expanded locally before being sent ✓.\n\nfn-cluster-up.sh: `worker \"podman exec '$FN_CONTAINER' ray start \\\n  --address='$FN_HEAD_IP:$FN_RAY_PORT' \\\n  --num-cpus '$RAY_NUM_CPUS'\" >/dev/null` — local expansion ✓.\n\nfn-cluster-down.sh: `residue=\"$(worker \"$(declare -f reap_serve_node); reap_serve_node\")\"` — worker() adds `|| true` to ssh; on ssh failure residue is empty → `[ \"${residue:-0}\" -eq 0 ]` ✓.\n\nOne issue in fn-cluster-down.sh: `source \"$SCRIPT_DIR/fn-env.sh\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true` — if fn-env.sh partially succeeds then fails on a rail FATAL (no rail), the FN_ variables set before the failure remain (sourcing runs to that point). The `: \"${FN_WORKER_HOST:=...}\"` fallback covers it ✓. Note: under set -u, unset variables used with := are fine.\n\nAlso in fn-cluster-down.sh, reap_serve_node uses `kill -TERM $pids` — unquoted is intentional ✓.\n\nUnit file: ExecStopPost double-invokes cluster-down (Stop + StopPost) — documented as idempotent ✓.\n\ntest_repo_invariants' secret scan: my files don't contain anything matching hf_/ghp_/AKIA/PRIVATE KEY ✓. GPL scan: no \"GNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE\" ✓.\n\nNow — one more consideration on claim 6.1 compliance: \"the unit file carries a stop-post teardown and no boot-time install, asserted by the tests suite\" ✓ test_unit_file_is_teardown_safe_and_boot_free.\n\nNow commit. Branch is already tally-work/flashnext-57f87640bc5b/host-tooling. Stage only my files (all inside conflictDomains): host/fn-env.sh, host/fn-cluster-up.sh, host/fn-cluster-down.sh, host/fn-preflight.sh, host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service, scripts/run-tp2.sh, tests/test_host_tooling.py.\n\nCommit message style: \"host-tooling: Pair-service orchestration: env doctrine, cluster up/down, first-light runner\". Might add a body detailing what landed. Recent commits appear to be subject-only (instruments:, container-recipe:). Keep subject + short body.\n\nLet me check git status first, and also verify that no stray scratch files exist in the worktree (results/receipts/preflight.json? no — my dry run used a sandbox). Verify: git status --porcelain.\n"}}
