{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"**Mission complete.** The `host-tooling` task is implemented, verified, and committed on the assigned lane.\n\n## What landed (commit `9686b7c` on `tally-work/flashnext-57f87640bc5b/host-tooling`, 7 files, all inside the conflict domains)\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `host/fn-env.sh` | Env doctrine: `PYTHONHASHSEED=0`, `PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85`, `HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT=1`, inductor/triton caches under `$FN_STATE_DIR` (never tmpfs), `VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_`, `VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1`, and a loud F.9 banner forbidding is-set-probe default exports |\n| `host/fn-cluster-up.sh` | Reap-then-gate on both nodes → containers via podman (worker over ssh on the **wire** `10.99.9.2`) → ray head+join with capped python pool → hard two-GPU gate → TP=2 eager serve + wait-for-reality API poll |\n| `host/fn-cluster-down.sh` | Idempotent both-node teardown, always exit 0 |\n| `host/fn-preflight.sh` | Byte-diff of both ranks' doctrine env, latency-hold device reads on both ends, per-rail link speeds, RTT probes on both rails vs the 200 µs budget → `preflight.json` |\n| `host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service` | oneshot + `RemainAfterExit`, `ExecStopPost` teardown, **no** install section |\n| `scripts/run-tp2.sh` | preflight → up → greedy 300-token byte-compare (`tp2.json`) → residency after 50 warmed decode tokens (`residency.json`) → fidelity losses + frontier logits under `results/fidelity/` (`fidelity.json`) → 262144-context probe (`context.json`) |\n| `tests/test_host_tooling.py` | 9 tests asserting the doctrine the grep gate can't catch |\n\n## The steer's semantic traps, handled and verified\n\n1. **`NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` computed from `ip -br addr`** — verified against the **live coordinator**: lists `thunderbolt0` (10.99.0.1/30), excludes `thunderbolt1` (169.254.200.164/16 link-local), logs the choice; auto-admits rail 1 when it gets a peer IP (simulated).\n2. **`NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1` unconditional** — bare export, asserted as such by test.\n3. **No probe-read defaults exported** — notably `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=0` (present in the donor env) was deliberately dropped per F.9.\n4. **Receipts match `receipts-verify.py` exactly** — validated with synthetic receipts both ways (pass path exit 0; a `null` table-residency probe correctly fails the gate).\n5. **Worker actions ride the wire** — ssh/ray dial `10.99.9.x` fleet identities, rails carry tensors only.\n6. **Reap-then-gate** — order enforced and asserted by test.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Task acceptance argv: **PASS** (bash -n ×6, all greps, 9 unit tests)\n- Full repo-tests gate: **29/29 OK** (including pre-existing invariants)\n- `receipts-verify.py`: clean (3 pre-existing receipts, 0 violations)\n- End-to-end preflight dry run (shimmed ssh/ip/ping/systemctl): fail and pass paths both behave; embedded Python blocks all compile\n\nNot pushed, not merged, no other worklist task read — the deterministic campaign nodes own those operations."}}
