ng VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=0 anywhere (donor had it; I deliberately dropped it).\n\n4. **Receipts match receipts-verify.py exactly** — let me simulate: create sample receipts for tp2/residency/fidelity/context in a scratch directory and run receipts-verify's checker against them? receipts-verify reads results/receipts in the repo. Can't drop test receipts in the repo (write boundary is tests/... results/ is actually outside the conflict domain! conflictDomains: host, scripts/run-tp2.sh, tests. Any path touched by any task commit must stay within those prefixes. Writing a sample receipt in results/ and then deleting it — \"every path touched by any task commit, including paths deleted later\" — only commit paths matter; uncommitted scratch files in the working tree are not committed. But safer to copy the repo elsewhere for simulation. Simulate receipts-verify against synthetic receipts in a temp copy.\n\n5. **Worker actions are over the wire** ✓ ssh 10.99.9.2; ray dials fleet IPs.\n\n6. **Reap-then-gate** ✓.\n\nAnother review point — the `worker()` helper in fn-cluster-up.sh uses `ssh \"$FN_WORKER_HOST\" \"$@\"` without error tolerance (set -e will fail if ssh fails — correct for up).\n\nfn-preflight.sh: `worker \"$(declare -f latency_hold_probe); latency_hold_probe\")\"` — ssh concatenates arguments; declare -f output is multi-line but fine as a single argument.\n\nPotential issue in fn-preflight.sh: `record \"rails_chosen\" \"$NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME\"` — NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME is set by sourcing fn-env.sh. OK.\n\nIn run-tp2.sh's residency heredoc: `subprocess.run([\"ssh\", WORKER, \"python3\", \"-\"], input=metrics_src.encode(), ...)` — good.\n\nPython issue in step tp2 heredoc: `data[\"preflight\"] = pre[\"data\"]` — preflight receipt's data contains a nested dict — JSON serializable ✓.\n\ncontext heredoc: `stream_options` include_usage — vLLM supports it for completions streaming on recent versions; pinned fork is vllm ~0.25 era; stream_options is supported since 0.4-ish. OK. Fallback: if usage is missing, decode_tps raises → fail receipt. Acceptable as honesty.\n\nAnother point to double-check: receipts-verify's `_context` uses `d.get(\"decode_ratio_vs_short_context\")` ✓ my key matches. `_tp2` uses `byte_identical_repeat` ✓. `_residency` uses `gtt_gib_per_rank`, `table_gpu_resident_bytes`, `read_after_warmed_decode` ✓ — my table_gpu_resident_bytes may be None → None != 0 → violation → graded fail. Intended honesty.\n\nNow, let me simulate receipts-verify against synthetic receipts in a temp copy to verify schema correctness.\n\nAlso let me smoke test fn-env.sh sourcing behavior on this machine in a modified env: create fake /sys? Can't. Instead, extract fn_choose_rails and run it against a fake `ip` shim to verify logic. Quick test:\n\nPATH shim: make a directory with an `ip` script responding to `-br -4 addr show dev thunderbolt0` → \"thunderbolt0 UP 10.99.0.1/30\" and thunderbolt1 → \"thunderbolt1 UP 169.254.5.6/16\". And fake /sys/class/net/thunderbolt{0,1} existence — the function checks /sys/class/net/$rail — can't fake without root... can we override? The check is a literal path. On this machine thunderbolt0 doesn't exist → both absent → chosen empty → FATAL. To test the parsing logic, just copy the function and manually source it in a shell with /sys/class/net overridden? Not easy. Instead, simulate with sed: temporarily replace \"/sys/class/net\" with a fake dir. Do it in a sandbox copy.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"All green. Now let me self-verify the steer's semantic traps functionally. First, simulate the rail-computation logic with a fake `ip` shim and fake sysfs:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2eac1abc5e9348d08b252a03","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"set -e; S=$(mktemp -d); cd \"$S\"\nmkdir -p sysnet/thunderbolt0 sysnet/thunderbolt1 bin\n# fake `ip`: rail0 has a routable /30, rail1 only link-local\ncat > bin/ip <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *thunderbolt0*) echo \"thunderbolt0  UP  10.99.0.1/30\" ;;\n  *thunderbolt1*) echo \"thunderbolt1  UP  169.254.5.6/16\" ;;\nesac\nEOF\nchmod +x bin/ip\n# sandbox copy of fn-env.sh with /sys/class/net redirected\nsed 's|/sys/class/net/|'\"$S\"'/sysnet/|g' /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling/host/fn-env.sh > fn-env-test.sh\nPATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$S/home\" bash -c \"source $S/fn-env-test.sh; echo RESULT=\\$NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME\" 2>&1\necho \"---- case 2: rail1 also gets a peer IP ----\"\ncat > bin/ip <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *thunderbolt0*) echo \"thunderbolt0  UP  10.99.0.1/30\" ;;\n  *thunderbolt1*) echo \"thunderbolt1  UP  10.99.4.1/30\" ;;\nesac\nEOF\nPATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$S/home\" bash -c \"source $S/fn-env-test.sh; echo RESULT=\\$NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME\" 2>&1 | tail -4\nrm -rf \"$S\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1459,"output":1754,"cacheRead":97280,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1261,"totalTokens":100493,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787989711122,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b045e437-7c98-4ac1-b486-264872f13cfb","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2eac1abc5e9348d08b252a03","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"fn-env: rail thunderbolt0 LISTED in NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME (10.99.0.1 is routable)\nfn-env: rail thunderbolt1 NOT listed (no routable peer IP; a peerless rail in NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME hangs RCCL bootstrap)\nRESULT=thunderbolt0\n---- case 2: rail1 also gets a peer IP ----\nfn-env: rail thunderbolt0 LISTED in NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME (10.99.0.1 is routable)\nfn-env: rail thunderbolt1 LISTED in NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME (10.99.4.1 is routable)\nRESULT=thunderbolt0,thunderbolt1\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787989752198},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The rail computation works as per steering: curre