), split(\"|\") → [\"unknown\"], then the `(u, v)` unpacking would fail. But check_hold always records. Still, as a defensive measure: unpack via partition. Fine to leave as-is — since it's always recorded. Actually, let's make it robust: the unpack `for n, (u, v) in hold.items()` in `{**{\"unit\": u...}` would crash if split returns a single element. Let's simplify with partition:\n\nhold = {}\nfor n in (...):\n    u, _, v = kv.get(\"hold_\"+n, \"unknown|unknown\").partition(\"|\")\n    hold[n] = {\"unit\": u, \"cpu_dma_latency\": v}\n\nLet me apply the patch to this python block for safety.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Hardening the preflight receipt builder against a malformed hold probe string:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6c3c06192aae4beeb1f32d35","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"kv = {}\nfor line in open(report):\n    if line.strip():\n        k, _, v = line.rstrip(\"\\n\").partition(\"\\t\")\n        kv[k] = v\nhold = {}\nfor n in (\"coordinator\", \"worker\"):\n    u, _, v = kv.get(\"hold_\" + n, \"unknown|unreadable\").partition(\"|\")\n    hold[n] = {\"unit\": u, \"cpu_dma_latency\": v}\nrails = {}","oldText":"kv = {}\nfor line in open(report):\n    if line.strip():\n        k, _, v = line.rstrip(\"\\n\").partition(\"\\t\")\n        kv[k] = v\nhold = {n: kv.get(\"hold_\" + n, \"unknown\").split(\"|\") for n in (\"coordinator\", \"worker\")}\nrails = {}"},{"newText":"           \"data\": {\"env_byte_diff\": kv.get(\"env_diff\"),\n                    \"rails_chosen\": kv.get(\"rails_chosen\", \"\").split(\",\"),\n                    \"latency_budget_us\": int(kv.get(\"budget_us\", \"200\")),\n                    \"latency_hold\": hold,\n                    \"rails\": rails}},","oldText":"           \"data\": {\"env_byte_diff\": kv.get(\"env_diff\"),\n                    \"rails_chosen\": kv.get(\"rails_chosen\", \"\").split(\",\"),\n                    \"latency_budget_us\": int(kv.get(\"budget_us\", 