of the report → receipt Python part of fn-preflight.sh. Either extract and run just the Python part with a synthetic report, or better yet, simulate the whole preflight on this machine using shims (ssh shim, fake sysfs, fake systemctl). This is heavier, but worthwhile since it lets us verify the script's plumbing (declare -f over ssh, record file, receipt JSON).\n\nPlan: create a sandbox PATH bin with the following:\n- ssh: runs the rest locally (exec bash -c \"$@\") — simulates a worker = same machine.\n- systemctl: prints \"active\" for is-active.\n- ping: prints canned stats.\n- ip: same shim as before.\n- od: prints 0.\n- sudo: exec \"$@\".\nFake /sys/class/net/thunderbolt0/speed — the check `[ -r /sys/class/net/$rail/speed ]` is a literal path again — can't be faked without sed. The rail_speeds function reads literal /sys/class/net — on this machine that results in \"absent\" — no problem, it gets recorded as absent. The RTT probe also uses a literal `ip -br -4 addr show dev thunderboltN` — but ip is shimmed, and the probe doesn't check for sysfs presence! rtt_probe_node runs `ip -br -4 addr show dev thunderbolt0` → shim returns an addr → pings the peer via the shimmed ping → records the rtt. The thunderbolt1 shim returns link-local → skipped as no-peer-ip.\n\n/dev/cpu_dma_latency: not readable by tom → falls back to `sudo -n od` → shim sudo → shim od prints 0. Actually, the [ -r /dev/cpu_dma_latency ] check is false → else branch with sudo -n od. Shim: `sudo` is exec \"${@#-n }\"... simplest is: cat > bin/sudo 'exec \"${@/-n/}\"' hmm. Let's just make sudo drop args: printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nshift\\nexec \"$@\"\\n' — sudo -n od ... → shift removes -n → exec od. Good.\n- od shim: regardless of args, prints \" 0\".\n\nThen run fn-preflight.sh with PATH override, RECEIPT → to a temp copy of the repo root? The script computes REPO_ROOT from SCRIPT_DIR/.. and writes to results/receipts/preflight.json — writing to results/ in the working tree is out of the write boundary for commits, but uncommitted scratch artifacts in the working tree pollute git status. Workaround: copy host/ into a sandbox directory structure $S/host + $S/results and run the copied script. The script is self-contained (sources fn-env.sh via SCRIPT_DIR).\n\nLet's run it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now an end-to-end dry run of `fn-preflight.sh` in a sandbox with shims for `ssh`, `ip`, `ping`, `systemctl`, `sudo`, `od`:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d37557d75ed0460aa1f8e5b5","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"set -e; S=$(mktemp -d); R=/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling\nmkdir -p \"$S/host\" \"$S/bin\"\ncp \"$R/host/fn-env.sh\" \"$R/host/fn-preflight.sh\" \"$S/host/\"\nsed -i 's|/sys/class/net/|'\"$S\"'/sysnet/|g' \"$S/host/fn-env.sh\"\nmkdir -p \"$S/sysnet/thunderbolt0\" \"$S/sysnet/thunderbolt1\"\ncat > \"$S/bin/ip\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *thunderbolt0*) echo \"thunderbolt0  UP  10.99.0.1/30\" ;;\n  *thunderbolt1*) echo \"thunderbolt1  UP  169.254.5.6/16\" ;;\nesac\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/ssh\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nshift; exec bash -c \"$*\"\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/systemctl\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n[ \"$1\" = is-active ] && echo active\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/ping\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\necho \"PING ignored\"; echo \"rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 58.0/77.2/112.0/9.1 ms\"\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/sudo\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nshift; exec \"$@\"\nEOF\ncat > \"$S/bin/od\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\necho \"           0\"\nEOF\nchmod +x \"$S/bin/\"*\nPATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$S/home\" bash \"$S/host/fn-preflight.sh\" 2>&1 | tail -12\necho \"=== receipt ===\"; cat \"$S/results/receipts/preflight.json\"\nrm -rf \"$S\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1729,"output":1160,"cacheRead":102400,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":614,"totalTokens":105289,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787989829059,"responseId":"chatcmpl-f170feef-41e1-47d0-b6b6-293825189159","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d37557d75ed0460aa1f8e5b5","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"fn-env: rail thunderbolt0 LISTED in NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME (10.99.0.1 is routable)\nfn-env: rail thunderbolt1 NOT listed (no routable peer IP; a peerless rail in NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME hangs RCCL bootstrap)\nfn-preflight: env byte-diff: both ranks carry identical doctrine env\nfn-preflight: latency hold on coordinator: held (device reads 0)\nfn-preflight: latency hold on worker: held (device reads 0)\nfn-preflight: FAIL: rtt on coordinator/thunderbolt0: 77200 us exceeds the 200 us budget\nfn-preflight: rtt on coordinator/thunderbolt1: no routable peer IP, not probed\nfn-preflight: FAIL: rtt on worker/thunderbolt0: 77200 us exceeds the 200 us budget\nfn-preflight: rtt on worker/thunderbolt1: no routable peer IP, not probed\nfn-preflight: receipt: /tmp/tmp.1OYFJ9Qsyb/results/receipts/preflight.json (status=fail)\n=== receipt ===\n{\n \"step\": \"preflight\",\n \"status\": \"fail\",\n \"ts\": \"2026-08-29T09:50:58\",\n \"data\": {\n  \"env_byte_diff\": \"pass\",\n  \"rails_chosen\": [\n   \"thunderbolt0\"\n  ],\n  \"latency_budget_us\": 200,\n  \"latency_hold\": {\n   \"coordinator\": {\n    \"unit\": \"active\",\n    \"cpu_dma_latency\": \"0\"\n   },\n   \"worker\": {\n    \"unit\": \"active\",\n    \"cpu_dma_latency\": \"0\"\n   }\n  },\n  \"rails\": {\n   \"thunderbolt0\": {\n    \"coordinator\": {\n     \"speed_mbps\": \"40000\",\n     \"rtt_us\": \"77200\"\n    },\n    \"worker\": {\n     \"speed_mbps\": \"40000\",\n     \"rtt_us\": \"77200\"\n    }\n   },\n   \"thunderbolt1\": {\n    \"coordinator\": {\n     \"speed_mbps\": \"40000\",\n     \"rtt_us\": \"no-peer-ip\"\n    },\n    \"worker\": {\n     \"speed_mbps\": \"40000\",\n     \"rtt_us\": \"no-peer-ip\"\n    }\n   }\n  }\n }\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787989858174},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plumbing works end-to-end: env-var byte diff, hold probe, link speed, RTT probe, receipt JSON. But my awk parse is exposing a bug:\n\nRTT: the ping shim outputs `rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 58.0/77.2/112.0/9.1 ms`. Expected average is 77.2 ms → 77200 µs? No wait — 77.2 ms = 77200 µs. But the actual fleet RTT is around 77 µs, not 77 ms! My shim wrote \"ms\" with the value 77.2 — in real ping, when the RTT is sub-millisecond, does it report e.g. `rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 0.058/0.077/0.112/0.009 ms`? ping prints in ms, and sub-ms values show as fractional ms like 0.077. The dotfiles sensor: `awk -F'[/ ]' '{ printf \"%d rtt 1\\n\", $8 * 1000 }'` — avg × 1000 → µs. Same as mine. So the parse is correct, and my shim was unrealistic (I wrote 77.2 ms instead of 0.077 ms). Not a bug.\n\nAlso note \"speed_mbps\": \"40000\" — this comes from the actual /sys/class/net/... wait, no, rail_speeds reads the literal /sys/class/net/$rail/speed — I didn't redirect this! This machine (tom's dev machine? no — the lane runs on the coordinator host... this shell is on the actual coordinator machine, and thunderbolt0 exists at 40000 Mb/s!). Interesting — the lane's shell runs directly on the coordinator, where thunderbolt0 exists. Good to know: /sys/class/net/thunderbolt0/speed = 40000. And for thunderbolt1 too... it also reported 40000 (present, negotiated). OK — that's the actual hardware under test. In that case, it might also be possible to source fn-env.sh on this machine and check the actual `ip` output! Let me test the actual rail computation on the coordinator (read-only).\n\nNote: the `speed_mbps` value type is a string inside the JSON — no problem for the record.\n\nLet me re-run the dry run with a realistic ping shim (0.077 ms) and confirm budget pass. Then test the actual fn-env.sh sourcing on this actual machine (the coordinator) — read-only, writes nothing other than mkdir of $HOME/.local/state/flashnext (harmless; that's a cache dir anyway; well, it creates a directory — tolerable? that's the intended state directory on this node; harmless). Actually, let me avoid side effects: set HOME to a temp dir and source the real fn-env.sh without the sysfs redirect. Real ip/iproute2 will show the real rail.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The plumbing works end-to-end (my shim's 77.2 *ms* was unrealistic — the actual fleet RTT is around 77 *µs*, which comes out as `0.077 ms` in the ping output, and `×1000 → µs` handles this correctly). Interestingly, this lane's shell is running on the actual coordinator — `thunderbolt0` exists at 40000 Mb/s. I'll verify by cross-checking against the **actual** `ip` output here, and re-run the dry run using realistic RTTs:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_39c4b24436e246beb87e201a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ip -br -4 addr show dev thunderbolt0 2>/dev/null; ip -br -4 addr show dev thunderbolt1 2>/dev/null; echo ---; HOME=$(mktemp -d) bash -c 'source /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling/host/fn-env.sh; echo \"REAL NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=$NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME\"; echo \"REAL NCCL_IB_DISABLE=$NCCL_IB_DISABLE\"; echo \"PYTHONHASHSEED=$PYTHONHASHSEED\"'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":4529,"output":951,"cacheRead":101376,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":669,"totalTokens":106856,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787989858180,"responseId":"chatcmpl-aeac5294-c5cd-41dc-bdb9-bbc1a6d8415d","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_39c4b24436e246beb87e201a","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"thunderbolt0     UP             10.99.0.1/30 \nthunderbolt1     UP             169.254.200.164/16 \n---\nfn-env: rail thunderbolt0 LISTED in NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME (10.99.0.1 is routable)\nfn-env: rail thunderbolt1 NOT listed (no routable peer IP; a peerless rail in NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME hangs RCCL bootstrap)\nREAL NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=thunderbolt0\nREAL NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1\nPYTHONHASHSEED=0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787989880240},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Verified on actual hardware: thunderbolt0 (10.99.0.1/30) is listed, thunderbolt1 (169.254.200.164/16, link-local, no peer) is correctly excluded. This is exactly the semantic trap the steer warned about, and it's handled properly.\n\nNext, quickly rerun the sandbox dry run with a realistic ping shim (average 0.077 ms) and confirm the pass path.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Real-hardware rail computation confirmed. Now the pass-path dry run with a realistic RTT:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c0fa2525c60e487d8792031d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"set -e; S=$(mktemp -d); R=/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling\nmkdir -p \"$S/host\" \"$S/bin\"; cp \"$R/host/fn-env.sh\" \"$R/host/fn-preflight.sh\" \"$S/host/\"\ncat > \"$S/bin/ip\" <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *thunderbolt0*) echo \"thunderbolt0  UP  10.99.0.1/30\" ;;\n  *thunderbolt1*) echo \"thunderbolt1  UP  169.254.5.6/16\" ;;\nesac\nEOF\nprintf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nshift; exec bash -c \"$*\"\\n' > \"$S/bin/ssh\"\nprintf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n[ \"$1\" = is-active ] && echo active\\n' > \"$S/bin/systemctl\"\nprintf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\necho \"rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 0.058/0.077/0.112/0.009 ms\"\\n' > \"$S/bin/ping\"\nprintf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\nshift; exec \"$@\"\\n' > \"$S/bin/sudo\"\nprintf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\necho \"           0\"\\n' > \"$S/bin/od\"\nchmod +x \"$S/bin/\"*\nPATH=\"$S/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$S/home\" bash \"$S/host/fn-preflight.sh\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"PREFLIGHT PASS-PATH OK\"\npython3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('$S/results/receipt